[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says "known: one issue, one fix queued". Its own table says otherwise.
It was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), so three
different bugs share one ticket. One fix will not close it.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket, with the reports it covers.
</Callout>

## The problems in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **`parser`** — the shared date parser reads every date month first. All our tenants write the day
  first, so bookings land with day and month swapped ("Booked for 2 March. The invite says 3 February").
  Fix in the parser: read dates in the tenant's locale.
- **`hint`** — booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants on
  booking-v3 (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) type what the hint says, and the form reads it
  the tenant's way. A parser fix does not touch this: the hint text and form must follow the locale.
- **`one-day`** — the date moves by one day, not by a swap: "Tuesday 12 May … Monday 11 May",
  "Every booking in June is one day off", "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."
  That is a time zone or daylight-saving bug, not a date-order one. The desk had already noted these
  reports (`desk-notes.json`); the #4471 table only footnotes them under `parser`. They have their own
  ticket, and they stay counted under `parser` too, where the desk files them by tenant.

## Outcome

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October.

- **`parser`** — fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Ticket closed as completed.
- **`hint`** — won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired. Ticket closed as not planned.
- **`one-day`** — no fix of its own in the update. The desk files these reports under `parser`, so the
  ticket is closed with #4471. If one-day moves keep coming after the parser fix, reopen it.

## How the counts were made

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so repeated rows count once.
- A report's problem comes from its tenant (locale and booking form) and its channel, as `causes.ts`
  does. Intake's `intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser and is not used.
- Counts follow the desk's own view, as exported (the #4471 table): each report under its tenant's
  cause. Reports the desk noted as a one-day move get their own row and ticket, and stay in `parser`.
- Every number on this page is computed from the export when the page is built (`#lib/kb/problems`).

## What to change on the desk

- Do not mark a big ticket "known" before its reports are read: #4471 held a fix and a won't-fix.
- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Subjects here cross
  all three problems, so the next decision record should merge on cause, not on subject.

